        "id": "p0",
        "title": "Recoil Armor",
        "text": "Recoil Armor flashes white: the armored character still takes your damage, but they don't flinch. Hits absorbed one by one don't add up to a real combo. The good news? A small set of attacks BREAKS armor outright - and a super with invincible startup doesn't fear what comes after the flash."
      },
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "title": "Answers",
        "text": "Here's the trick: hitting armor doesn't count as a real hit, but some moves are allowed to jump-cancel even on armor - Mizuka {input:5A} is one of them. Against Rumi's slow armored {input:41236C}, tag the armor with {input:5A}, then jump-cancel so her ground command throw grabs nothing but air."
      }
    ],
